<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25891" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">largĭtas</span></b> , ātis,
			f.
		1. largus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abundance, bounty, liberality</i> (rare but
			class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">largitas nimia, opp. parsimonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 3, 1, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae istaec subita est largitas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ad. 5, 9, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tui muneris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 4, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra fruges cum maxima largitate fundit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 2, 62, 156</span></i>
			.</div>
